Z||000000||3fifty||05-06-2001||03:01 AM||||1985 GT-V6 smokes a little only on start up. I know that with the 350's ect. smoke at start up is usually valve seals. Is this true with the 2.8 also? Has anyone used a product that would help this problem without<BR>going inside the motor?||||reg||5
Z||000001||GoCartGuy||05-06-2001||06:00 AM||||What color smoke? Blue or white? How much? How many miles?  Any engine work done recently?  What weight oil are you running?<P><P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||05-06-2001||07:52 AM||||I wouldnt worry, my V6 has smoked for a second or 2 since new on startup. I cant make it use ANY oil between changes. FieroLisas GT is same way too. Most Ive seen do too, just one of those little Fiero quirks I guess.<P>Quote of the day =<BR> IF IT AINT BROKE...DONT FIX IT !!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||hugh||05-06-2001||08:54 AM||||With any engine that is an indication the valve seals are not perfect.When the engine is off some oil runs down the valve stems and is drawn into the cylinders on startup.When you see the smoke it shouldn't last more than a few seconds.It is nothing to worry about!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrgone||05-06-2001||10:26 AM||||if it aint broke, fix it till it is||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||05-06-2001||05:55 PM||||good one mrgone, lol. unfortunately, a lot of people do that. heres a perfect story. I was at Buckeye Lake a couple of summers ago. This guy had a sweet Tahiti Jet Cruiser prob like 28-30 footer. he had a problem and thought to save time trying to fix his drive in the water, hed just put it on his trailer and fix it. so he backed his car (caddy) and trailer down the ramp and then powered his boat quick to get it on. He misjudged and ran the side of the bow into the end of the boards on trailer, making a 2' square hole below the waterline. he backed it back off and in the confusion the guy got out of the car to help, letting the trailer and car roll back and completly submerge. now they had nothing to do but run the now fast sinking boat up on the concrete ramp. All this because he thought he could adjust the jet drive better for a little more speed.||||reg||1
